      "classification": "different_products_origins_or_programs",
      "reason": "Claim 1 cites a 25% tariff on UK steel/aluminum articles and derivatives, while Claim 2 cites a 15% tariff on the same product category from the UK. The context indicates these are distinct rate tiers within a conditional structure (e.g., 'unless a lower rate applies'), where the 15% rate likely applies to specific derivative sub-categories or conditions not fully detailed in the first claim's summary, rather than a direct contradiction of the base rate.",
      "verification_question": "Does the 15% rate apply exclusively to specific steel/aluminum derivatives under Annex I-B/C, while the 25% rate applies to other articles or non-derivative products?"
